From naomi at stat.psu.edu  Mon Jun  6 16:22:08 2005
From: naomi at stat.psu.edu (Naomi Altman)
Date: Mon Jun  6 16:24:13 2005
Subject: [BioC] Analyzing mulitple tissues
In-Reply-To: <42A42E6D.2030506@netvision.net.il>
References: <s2a40ba6.096@UWCMCM1P.UWCM.AC.UK>
	<42A42E6D.2030506@netvision.net.il>
Message-ID: <6.2.1.2.2.20050606101526.03bc8c08@imap.stat.psu.edu>

Biological inference implies that the "signal" can be observed above the 
biological variation.  If you have no biological replicates, you cannot 
determine if your signal is higher than the biological variation.

So, there is no statistically valid means of analyzing your data that 
improves on an arbitrary choice of "fold difference", such as 2-fold 
difference.


