This is indeed not working correctly.

Try selecting "Other Repository" and then in the field that pops up  
right next to it: http://www.bioconductor.org

Select "Binary Format Packages" if you want to install binaries, else  
it will install source format.

Press "Get List"

Select package or (all) packages and press "Install Selected"

Rob

Note:  Binaries have been built for the CRAN version of R. If you did  
a vanilla install from CRAN it will work.
             If you did build R on Tiger with gcc 4.0, you will have  
to install from source.


