Subject: [BioC] What's the meaning of "covar" in the widget of ReadAffy
 and	how to determine this value?
In-Reply-To: <20050615181033.28807.qmail@web52308.mail.yahoo.com>
References: <20050615181033.28807.qmail@web52308.mail.yahoo.com>
Message-ID: <42B1BB4D.4030800@med.umich.edu>

Elaine yang wrote:
> Hi there, I am new in using package and some basic questions for
> ReadAffy. I tried to use ReadAffy(widget=TRUE) function to select the
> cel files by using widget tools. But after I select all the cel
> files, it goes to create the phenodata step. What's the meaning of
> "covar" and how to choose the value of covariate?

The covariate is a descriptive term used to distinguish one sample from 
another. For instance, let's say you have an experiment where you are 
comparing rat liver tumors vs normal liver after treatment with a 
chemotherapeutic agent. You would have (at least) two covariate names 
here. An example of what the covariates would look like is this:

Sample	Treatment	Type
1	Chemo		Tumor
2	Chemo		Normal
3	None		Tumor
4	None		Normal

Does that help?

Best,

Jim


